<Window x:Class="DCST4.HelpWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Width="680"
        Height="640"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner">
    <FlowDocumentScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
        <FlowDocument FontFamily="Segoe UI" FontSize="13" PagePadding="20" TextAlignment="Left">
            <FlowDocument.Resources>
                <Style x:Key="H" TargetType="Paragraph">
                    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16"/>
                    <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
                    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF1F3A5F"/>
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,14,0,4"/>
                </Style>
            </FlowDocument.Resources>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Quick start</Paragraph>
            <List>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Enter the server's AE title, host and port under Server. Try Ping and Dicom Echo.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Under Exam, select the modality (CT, MR, CR, DX, US, XA, RF, MG, PT or NM) and exam type, and how many images you want. 1 series with 1 image gives a single test image.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Click Generate &amp; Send, and follow each image in the Results tab.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Look the exam up in the PACS viewer. To compare the image with the tags, turn on burned-in text under File &gt; Settings first.</Paragraph></ListItem>
            </List>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Burned-in text</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>By default the images have no burned-in patient details. Under File &gt; Settings, on the Burned-in text tab, you can turn on a black text box in the upper left corner of each image and tick which tags it shows. The values are read from the image's own tags. Burned In Annotation is YES when text is drawn, otherwise NO. The diagonal TEST IMAGE watermark is always there.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Auto and manual values</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Everything on the Identifiers tab is generated by default, and the fields show what the next run will use. Untick Auto to enter your own value. Auto values are drawn when the program starts and when you click New values, and they stay on screen after a run so you can look the exam up in PACS. The values a run used are also written to the Log tab.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Running again without New values uses the same patient, accession number and Study UID, so the images arrive as a new series in the same study, also if you changed modality or exam type. Series numbers start at 1 again, and an Auto Study Date/Time is the time of each run. Click New values to start a separate study. To draw new values after every run instead, tick Draw new Auto values after each run under File &gt; Settings.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>A manual Series UID requires exactly one series, and a manual SOP Instance UID exactly one image, because these must be unique.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Additional tags</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Under File &gt; Settings, on the Additional tags tab, you can add tags on top of the fixed fields. Each one gets a row on the Identifiers tab, where you can untick Auto and type a value for the session.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Common tags are ticked in a list, and Auto generates their values. A custom tag is entered as (0008,1070), 00081070 or a keyword such as OperatorsName, and Auto uses the default value you enter. An empty default sends the tag empty. Separate several values with a backslash where the tag allows it.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>A private tag, one with an odd group number, also needs a private creator and a VR. A custom tag can replace a generated value such as Manufacturer, but not one that would break the image or remove its marking as a test image. The message says why when a tag cannot be added.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Patient IDs</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Random Patient IDs only ever come from Skatteverket's official list of test personnummer, built into the program. Birth date and sex are taken from the number. The list also holds future dates and people born in the 1890s, so random selection is limited to the age range below the fields, 0 to 100 by default.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If you enter a Patient ID that is not on the list, the program warns you. It is still used, but make sure it is not a real person's number.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Names with å, ä, ö</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>About 40% of random names contain å, ä or ö. Select the Specific Character Set under Exam: ISO_IR 100 (Latin-1), ISO_IR 192 (UTF-8) or Empty value. A manual value that the selected set cannot represent stops the run with a message, rather than being sent wrong.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Empty value sends the tag with zero length, which means Basic ASCII (ISO 646). Random names then lose their å, ä and ö, so Åström becomes Astrom. A strict validator may object to the empty tag, since Specific Character Set should have a value when it is present.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If the viewer shows Ã¥ instead of å, the system has read UTF-8 text as Latin-1. With burned-in text turned on, the text in the image shows what was intended.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Transfer syntax and fallback</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The images are sent in the selected transfer syntax. fo-dicom also always proposes Implicit VR in a presentation context of its own, as DICOM expects. Each context is shown in the Log tab with the server's answer.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If the server does not accept the selected syntax, the run stops with an error and nothing is sent, so a test of JPEG Lossless can not pass by accident. Tick Allow fallback to Implicit VR to send as Implicit VR instead, as a real modality would. The run then finishes with a warning, and the Syntax used column shows what was really sent.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Reading the results</Paragraph>
            <Table CellSpacing="4">
                <Table.Columns>
                    <TableColumn Width="110"/>
                    <TableColumn/>
                </Table.Columns>
                <TableRowGroup>
                    <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph>Success</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Status 0x0000. The server has taken responsibility for the image.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFFF4C2"><TableCell><Paragraph>Warning</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Stored, but the server changed or dropped something. For example 0xB000 coercion, 0xB006 elements discarded, 0xB007 data set does not match the SOP class.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFAD4D0"><TableCell><Paragraph>Failure</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Not stored. For example 0xA7xx out of resources, 0xA9xx data set does not match, 0xCxxx cannot understand. The run continues with the next image.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFE6E6E6"><TableCell><Paragraph>NotSent</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>No response for this image, for example because the association was rejected, aborted or timed out. The description says why.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                </TableRowGroup>
            </Table>
            <Paragraph>Vendor-specific codes keep their real value in the Status column. The status bar shows the totals and throughput of the last run. Images never generated because the run stopped early have no row, but are counted as not sent in the totals.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Running tests against a PACS</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>On the Tests tab below the exam settings, tick the tests and click Run tests. They run against the destination entered under Server. Select a row to see its explanation and the steps of the association, with the raw status of each response. Cancel stops the run, and what was finished is still saved.</Paragraph>
            <Table CellSpacing="4">
                <Table.Columns>
                    <TableColumn Width="130"/>
                    <TableColumn/>
                </Table.Columns>
                <TableRowGroup>
                    <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph>PASS</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>The system did what the test expects.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFAD4D0"><TableCell><Paragraph>FAIL</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>It answered, refused or broke off in a way the test does not accept.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFFF4C2"><TableCell><Paragraph>NOT_SUPPORTED</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>It said it does not support this, for example by not accepting the SOP class.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph>EXPECTED_FAILURE</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>It refused something it is supposed to refuse.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFE6E6E6"><TableCell><Paragraph>TIMEOUT</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>No connection, association or response within the timeout under File &gt; Settings.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFE6E6E6"><TableCell><Paragraph>INDETERMINATE</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>The test could not reach a verdict, for example because the run was cancelled.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFAD4D0"><TableCell><Paragraph>TOOL_ERROR</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>A bug or local problem in this program, such as a missing client certificate. Not the fault of the PACS.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                </TableRowGroup>
            </Table>
            <Paragraph>Each run is saved as a JSON file with full detail and a CSV file with one row per result, in the folder on the tab. The client certificate thumbprint is never written to them.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The same tests can run from the command line with DCST4.Cli.exe, which is in the program's folder. Click Save profile as JSON to write the destination to a file, and then run: DCST4.Cli.exe run --profile target.json --tests c-echo --out C:\Temp\results. The exit code is 0 with no FAIL or TOOL_ERROR, 1 with at least one of those, 2 for bad arguments or an unusable profile, and 130 if cancelled with Ctrl+C.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">What the PACS supports</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The negotiation probe on the Tests tab finds out what the destination supports from association negotiation alone. No images are sent. For each SOP class it proposes every transfer syntax in a presentation context of its own, split over several associations since one can hold at most 128 contexts.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The result is on the Capabilities tab, one row per SOP class and one column per transfer syntax. Rest the mouse on a cell to see the full answer, and on a column heading for the full name. Save as JSON or CSV writes the table, and every run also saves it next to the result files. The tab also shows what the destination identified itself as and its maximum PDU length.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Load claimed reads a JSON file of what the vendor's Conformance Statement claims, in the same layout as the saved matrix, and lists what was claimed but rejected, accepted but not claimed, and claimed but never answered.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Three more tests check refusals: an unknown calling AE title, a wrong called AE title, and an association with only unsupported contexts. EXPECTED_FAILURE means the destination refused as it should. A destination that accepts an unknown AE title gets FAIL, as a finding to report and not as a fault in this program.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Test datasets</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>DCST4.Cli.exe can write reproducible test data: DCST4.Cli.exe generate --dataset ct --out C:\Temp\ct --seed 42. The same seed gives the same files, with a manifest.json of hashes that can be compared later. DCST4.Cli.exe list-datasets shows the dataset types, which include multi-frame images, reports, documents and presentation states, and list-codecs shows which compressions work.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Patient IDs always come from the list of test personnummer. The name is a Swedish name by default. To mark every test patient as DCST4^TEST^number instead, choose it on the Identifiers tab under File &gt; Settings, or use --patient-naming MarkedTestName on the command line. This setting does not affect Generate &amp; Send. No test on the Tests tab uses datasets yet, so it has no visible effect in the program until one does.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Saving to disk</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Tick Save to disk, with or without Send to server. The folder becomes a DICOM File-set that viewers can open: a DICOMDIR at the top, and the images in DICOM\EX000001\S001\IM0001 in the selected transfer syntax. DICOM limits these names to 8 characters and no extension, so the folders do not show patient details. The Saved to column shows where each image went.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Each run gets a new EX folder and nothing is overwritten. Saving again to the same folder adds to the same DICOMDIR. Each file is saved before it is sent, so it exists even if sending fails, and the DICOMDIR is written when the run ends, also if it stopped early.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Version check</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>When the program starts it asks GitHub for the latest release, and opens a window if there is a new version, with a link and the release notes. You only see this window when a new version was found: if GitHub cannot be reached, for example on a closed network, the program carries on and says nothing. To turn it off, untick the box on the Updates tab under File &gt; Settings, and nothing is sent at startup.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Opening Help &gt; About also asks GitHub and shows the result in the window, including if the check failed. Nothing is downloaded or installed.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Logs and settings</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The Log tab shows this program's messages, and the complete log is in File &gt; Open log directory (%LocalAppData%\DCST4\Logs). The command line program logs to Cli files in the same folder. Settings are stored in %LocalAppData%\DCST4\user.config.</Paragraph>
        </FlowDocument>
    </FlowDocumentScrollViewer>
</Window>
